id: pm-rl-a2zp
title: "Lift the prefix learner's capacity bound: content-addressed checkpoint artifacts instead of the 4096-byte staging record"
description: "Follow-up to pm-rl-prefix and PR 86 only; no capacity changes in that PR. Its honest null is bounded by one SGD pass, at most 512 training rows, hashing width at most 64, and quantized weights constrained by the 4096-byte staging record. Retained policies predict only slow. Separate checkpoint artifact storage from the staging receipt to permit a larger bounded learner."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-18T20:01:33.655Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T19:37:26.782Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T19:37:20.864Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T19:37:20.864Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Store the checkpoint as a content-addressed blob referenced by digest from the receipt; Keep the budget and promotion gate unchanged; Rerun live acceptance on the same sealed dataset and report majority baseline, prediction diversity, held-out gain and confidence bound, and final-test before and after honestly"
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[34]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T20:02:54.247Z",codex-agent,"Tracking only, requested during PR 86 review. Same parent as pm-rl-prefix. No artifact storage, learner, budget or promotion-gate change is included in the review fix. Current null result and capacity constraints are recorded in docs/history-prefix.md and docs/prefix-live-evidence.json."
  "2026-10-21T04:40:54.170Z",codex-agent,"Read the queue rules, no-git audit and related prefix/RSI items. Implement immutable SHA-256 checkpoint blobs with atomic publication, typed integrity failures and a reachability ledger shared with garbage collection. Keep staging receipts bounded and store references in durable controller receipts. Prove a larger bounded prefix learner through promotion/resume on real plain-directory trackers and concurrent processes. Measure the same pinned public corpus before/after; preserve the statistical gate and report null improvement honestly. Dependency pins stay unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T04:50:15.966Z",codex-agent,"Artifact store and process/controller integration are implemented. Initial focused checks pass 3/3 for existing fitting, promotion and receipt validation; lint, zero duplication and docstrings pass (45 sources, 330 declarations). New plain-directory tests exercise a 4096-weight learner and independent concurrent promoters. Their restricted PATH must retain OS process-start tooling (getconf/ps) while omitting git; the first run correctly refused an unverifiable lease, and the fixture now preserves that required tooling. Existing 4096-byte storage reservations remain unchanged for widths through 64; opting into larger widths requires a separate 1 MiB storage reservation from the existing approval, with no compute or statistical threshold change."
  "2026-10-21T04:53:45.821Z",codex-agent,"Capacity and concurrency acceptance passes 3/3 on real plain-directory SDK trackers: a 4096-weight checkpoint is promoted, interruption resumes with five total fits, completed replay launches none, corrupt/missing artifacts refuse with typed errors and unchanged jobs, and two independent processes promote the same immutable checkpoint with both ledger roots retained. The restricted PATH contains Node and OS process-start tools but no git executable. A fourth regression now exercises the reproducible corpus benchmark, plus explicit staging-size and completed-artifact recovery refusals. Full gates and public-corpus measurements follow."
  "2026-10-21T05:03:02.116Z",codex-agent,"The artifact module passes focused real-tracker integrity/fault tests at 100 percent lines, branches and functions, including a failed hard-link publication and corrupt-ledger refusal before deletion. Expanded integration coverage hit the new test's initial five-minute timeout while several training checks overlapped; that run is failed evidence. The new integration fixtures now have a bounded fifteen-minute allowance, matching the linked-test watchdog. Existing package gate thresholds and existing regression deadlines remain unchanged. A preliminary public benchmark was stopped after source refinements; only a frozen-source completed repetition will be published."
  "2026-10-21T05:08:38.141Z",codex-agent,"Six isolated behavioral reverts all typecheck and fail retained regressions with exit 1: restore validatePrefixKnobs, restore runPrefixTrainer with its required crypto import, restore withRlController, disable exact-byte SHA verification, disable unreachable collection, and replace exclusive publication with overwriting writes. Restored production passes the capacity regression 1/1 (290840.755645 ms including module startup), and the artifact/fault suite passes 2/2 at 100/100/100 measured lines/branches/functions. The public corpus rebuilt to digest 6eb9e7dcb22bb243b472512ce55e4c0ab1d2fa6053b5d489eea7b59240592f48: 25 repositories, split counts 943/225/214/385. A fresh frozen-source measurement is running sequentially. The earlier linked run is failed evidence (two passes, one failure, one cancellation); its new integration deadline and fixture deadline are now aligned at fifteen minutes."
  "2026-10-21T05:18:06.413Z",codex-agent,"Plain-directory controller regression passes 1/1 and counts zero Git invocations. Removing only the filesystem guard typechecks and fails it with exit 1, giving seven behavioral revert proofs in docs/checkpoint-revert-evidence.json. Worktree launch fencing remains available when repository metadata exists. The benchmark normalizes relative scratch coordinates before SDK initialization and its evidence excludes checkpoint payload arrays. Public measurements now use fresh independent trackers outside the checkout. Reproduced the separate dataset-builder missing-repository diagnostic gap on three real temporary SDK trackers and created follow-up pm-rl-nogitdata; provenance restrictions remain unchanged. No upstream CLI/SDK issue was filed."
  "2026-10-21T05:24:47.007Z",codex-agent,"Frozen-source public corpus experiment completes both two-generation K=2 programmes with five fits each and unchanged replay. Fitted sizes: legacy-capacity widths 296-651 bytes; expanded capacity 10343-18756 bytes. Initial checkpoints are 396 and 17921 bytes. Median verified warm load (100 iterations): legacy reader 0.039227 ms; artifact reader at width 32 0.041579 ms; artifact reader at width 4096 3.768197 ms. Large blobs are refused by the legacy 4096-byte reader. Source hashes match all eleven recorded files. Both real-data runs are honest nulls: retained meta 140/214, gain 0, lower bound -0.21778781183411927; final before/after 220/385, matching majority, one predicted class and p=1. No public-data learner or recipe promotes. The synthetic real-tracker positive promotion/resume proof remains separate. Measurements and digests exclude payload arrays and raw examples."
  "2026-10-21T05:34:59.781Z",codex-agent,"PR 92 is open at source commit f8b98453b714717a857ce6a646fc1d979bc1ab98. The required linked command node --test test/checkpoint-artifacts.test.ts passes 6/6 through pinned pm test --run --progress on Node 26 with the snapshot/no-PM-context configuration: zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, 319882 ms. This includes positive larger-learner promotion/resume, integrity refusal, relative-coordinate benchmark, zero-Git controller, publication fault and concurrent writer acceptance. Complete unchanged npm/Bun CI gates are progressing; fresh-checkout tracker health and CodeQL pass. Normal local health still reports host-version skew and merge-fence drift; these remain separate and are not repaired in this feature. Automated review is unavailable from Greptile (trial ended), Sourcery (quota) and CodeRabbit (automatic review skipped); summaries are not approvals."
  "2026-10-21T05:49:21.901Z",codex-agent,"First source-head CI runs every behavioral test successfully: npm Node 26 and Bun Node 26 each pass 661/661 with zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, but correctly fail the unchanged 100 percent branch gate at 99.98 percent overall (process.ts 99.70 percent). The missing case is the combined artifact-plus-staging allowance: the earlier test exhausted the artifact's own allowance first. Strengthened real-filesystem checks now require the combined-budget refusal specifically, at one byte below total retained storage. The focused trainer IO test passes directly 1/1 and through pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress 1/1. Disabling only the combined-budget check typechecks and fails that retained test (exit 1), giving eight revert proofs. Production source and all eleven public-measurement hashes are unchanged. Stopped the superseded local full gate after its known coverage gap was established; it is not passing evidence. Rerunning the complete unchanged CI matrix after the test-only fix."
  "2026-10-21T06:08:13.970Z",codex-agent,"Complete source/test-head validation PASS at f3c8e06d37e715ab4bb65d45c7cc92ed6e911582: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/39551781806 . npm run release:check on Node 22 and Node 26 and bun run release:check on Node 26 each pass 661/661, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo; all 46 sources have statements/lines/branches/functions 100/100/100/100; all 334 declarations are documented. Full logs confirm typecheck/build/lint/zero duplication/attestation/identity/zero production vulnerabilities/pack/changelog/Bun graph checks and strict fresh-checkout tracker health. The merge checkout tree matches the source head. CodeQL run 39551782330 passes. Linked PM commands pass 6/6 and 1/1; all eight typechecked behavioral reverts fail. Larger checkpoints train and promote on synthetic real trackers, resume/replay from verified digests, and survive concurrent promotion. Public corpus sizes/load times and its honest null are recorded separately. Normal local health advisories and unavailable substantive reviews remain explicit. Follow-up pm-rl-nogitdata stays open. Releasing the claim without closing, merging or releasing the package; the final evidence-only commit will receive its own CI verification."
  "2026-10-21T06:44:28.327Z",codex-agent,"PR 92 review round: fetched all four unresolved threads and all their comments; latest CodeRabbit review contains no Outside diff range section. All four findings are valid: validate policy schema and semantic identity before publication, prevent mixed Git executable availability from splitting worktree authority, clarify the width-64 storage threshold, and discover process tools from PATH. Branch already includes main. Will add retained regression tests and isolated behavioral revert proofs, self-review the complete diff for the same defect classes, and run unchanged npm/Bun release gates with isolated Git identity. Dependency pins remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T06:48:02.216Z",codex-agent,"Focused review regressions pass 5/5: invalid prefix/improver rejection before any publication and healthy GC afterward; mixed Git availability across real worktrees enforces both active-controller and launch-elsewhere refusals; synthetic PATH discovery catches hardcoded process-tool locations; README width-64 reservation contract; standalone operation without Git probes. Shared authority now reads gitdir/commondir metadata directly and fails closed on corrupt real-worktree pointers. Self-review covered every changed production integration and both restricted-PATH setup sites. No additional policy-publication or approval-threshold instances found. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication and docstrings pass; new authority fault branches are being exercised before full gates."
  "2026-10-21T06:49:52.111Z",codex-agent,"Four isolated behavioral reverts all typecheck and fail their retained regression with exit 1: encodeCheckpointArtifacts without policy validation misses the expected rejection; acquireControllerLease with the prior Git-failure fallback actually executes the peer controller instead of refusing; checkpointToolBin with hardcoded tool paths fails synthetic PATH assertions; the previous README fails the width-64 storage contract. Restored focused checks passed 5/5. Detailed commands and timings are appended to docs/checkpoint-revert-evidence.json. Reverts were performed only in isolated source copies; the package worktree was never reverted."
  "2026-10-21T07:10:37.672Z",codex-agent,"PR 92 review round complete at source head 6bfa3bcc765d96d67adba1da3bf85d4b66b491f5. All four unresolved findings were valid and fixed; thread ids map to function-level revert receipts in docs/checkpoint-revert-evidence.json. Full unchanged CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/39558157659 passes npm run release:check on Node 22 and Node 26 and bun run release:check on Node 26: each 665/665, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, all 46 sources at 100 percent statements/lines/branches/functions, 336 documented declarations. Tracker health, typecheck/build/lint, zero duplication, attestation, identity, zero production vulnerabilities, pack dry-run, changelog and Bun installation pass. CodeQL run 39558157708 passes. Pinned linked focused test passes 5/5; all four new isolated reverts typecheck and fail their retained tests. The provider interruption stopped the local full gate; it is incomplete evidence, not a passing result or a local timeout. No new CLI/SDK defect found. Source, thresholds and dependency pins are unchanged by this final evidence update. No thread replies/resolutions, mentions, merge or release. Leaving the item in progress for orchestrator verification and releasing its claim."
  "2026-10-21T07:42:42.696Z",codex-agent,"PR 92 review round: fetched all five threads and every comment; exactly one remains unresolved (PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6uqs1G). Latest substantive CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Remote branch is current and contains main. Confirmed inspectCheckpointArtifact unnecessarily certifies every ledger blob. Plan: structurally validate ledger references, verify only requested blob for inspection, preserve full certification before GC, and add real non-Git tracker regressions with behavioral revert proof. Reviewing the complete PR diff for the same unnecessary global-read coupling."
  "2026-10-21T07:45:16.161Z",codex-agent,"Implemented PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6uqs1G: inspection verifies ledger JSON hashes and reference structure, then reads and validates only its requested blob. Full ledger certification and fail-closed GC remain unchanged. Whole-PR call-site review confirms the show command delegates here, resume/replay and process reads use specific references, and GC is the only production consumer requiring full certification. Added object validation for malformed references found during structural-reader review. Three real plain-directory tracker regressions pass. Revert proof: replacing only inspectCheckpointArtifact lookup with readCheckpointLedger typechecks and fails 2/3 retained tests (unrelated corrupt blob blocks inspection; duplicate roots read target three times rather than once). Removing only validateReference object guard typechecks and fails 1/3 with raw TypeError. Both variants restored; commands and timings retained in docs/checkpoint-revert-evidence.json."
  "2026-10-21T07:59:46.203Z",codex-agent,Focused inspection regressions pass 3/3 directly and through the pinned pm linked-test runner. Both behavioral revert variants typecheck and fail retained regressions as recorded in the receipt. The isolated-identity npm full gate is progressing without reported failures on the shared host. Publishing this source checkpoint now so the existing CI matrix can run complete npm gates on Node 22 and 26 and the complete Bun gate on Node 26 in parallel; final gate counts will be recorded after verification. No thresholds or workflow settings changed.
  "2026-10-21T08:18:54.797Z",codex-agent,"Verified source head 913c6d8161cf457aade70312cdced0b07223bef4 in CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/39565988092: npm run release:check on Node 22 and Node 26, plus bun run release:check on Node 26, each passes 668/668 tests with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos. All four coverage dimensions are 100% across all 46 sources; all 336 declarations documented. Unchanged lint, duplication, release-attestation, strict fresh-checkout tracker health, identity audit, zero-vulnerability production audit, packaging, changelog and Bun package-graph installation pass. CodeQL run 39565988276 passes. Local full npm run was intentionally stopped with exit 143 after all three CI gates passed to avoid redundant shared-host work; it is not passing evidence, and no local timeout was observed. Final follow-up changes only docs and tracker evidence, preserving tested executable source, tests and gate configuration. Only PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6uqs1G remains unresolved by request; no replies or resolutions posted. No new PM CLI/SDK defect encountered. Final-head substantive review remains pending; no merge or release."
  "2026-10-21T08:43:06.583Z",codex-agent,"PR 92 descriptor review: remote head is current and contains main. Fetched all review threads with every comment and pagination confirmed complete; sole unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6ur6XM is valid. Latest substantive CodeRabbit body has no Outside diff range findings. Replace path-based stat/read with one no-follow descriptor, descriptor metadata checks and bounded reads, including same-inode growth. Add real plain-directory tracker race and error regressions, behavioral revert proof, whole-diff review for related read races, and unchanged npm/Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-21T08:47:21.072Z",codex-agent,"Fixed PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6ur6XM: readVerifiedFile opens once with O_NOFOLLOW and O_NONBLOCK, validates fstat metadata and reads at most the validated size plus one byte. Exact-size and digest checks reject same-inode growth, truncation and corruption; finally closes on success, metadata failure and IO failure. Three new real non-Git tracker tests cover pathname replacement by oversized files, symlinks and directories, bounded growth/truncation, short reads and descriptor cleanup. Seven focused regressions pass directly and through pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress. Isolated function-level reverts both typecheck: old path-stat/read fails 3/3; descriptor plus unbounded read fails the growth regression (1/3). Exact commands and timings are recorded in docs/checkpoint-revert-evidence.json. Whole-PR review confirms every immutable blob, ledger and publication-collision read shares the fixed helper, including inspection, GC, resume/replay and trainer artifact hydration. Existing thresholds and dependency pins are unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T08:51:56.920Z",codex-agent,"Additional same-class self-review fix: the benchmark legacy comparison used readFileSync after trusting only reference metadata. It now uses the same descriptor-bound reader through an internal export, retaining its SHA and policy checks. A real non-Git tracker regression requires an oversized replacement to fail with a typed refusal before any bytes are read. Reverting only measureCheckpointLoads to its prior raw read typechecks and fails this retained regression (exit 1, 5.719 seconds). Restored focused checks pass 8/8. Historical timing receipts remain explicitly tied to their recorded source revision. GitHub full-gate jobs are queued; final full npm/Bun results will be recorded after completion."
  "2026-10-21T08:55:46.428Z",codex-agent,"Final benchmark review removes its redundant SHA pass because readVerifiedFile already verifies exact bytes; both comparison readers retain one byte-digest verification. Re-ran the self-review revert by restoring the entire prior measureCheckpointLoads function with its required imports: typecheck passes and the oversized-baseline regression fails (exit 1, 8.598 seconds). Source-only correction supersedes the local npm gate while it was in integration coverage; that run was deliberately stopped, is incomplete evidence, and is not a timeout or a pass. Restarting full gates on the final source. All historical receipts remain unchanged except the latest proof timing."
  "2026-10-21T09:22:20.620Z",codex-agent,"Verified final executable source 6759e6ab63f151ae720af5e127776d52a17fb8c7 in CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/39573073353: npm run release:check and bun run release:check on Node 26 each pass 672/672, with zero fail/skip/cancel/todo and 100 percent statements/lines/branches/functions across all 46 sources. All 336 declarations documented; unchanged identity, zero duplication, zero production vulnerabilities, packaging, changelog, strict tracker health and Bun installation checks pass. CodeQL run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/39573073352 passes. Node 22 release variant is still running. The redundant local Node 26 npm full gate was stopped with exit 143 after both required CI runtime variants passed, so it is incomplete evidence and not counted as passing. No local timeout was observed. Final documentation and claim release follow the remaining CI result."
  "2026-10-21T09:25:20.616Z",codex-agent,"Final validation complete at executable source 6759e6ab63f151ae720af5e127776d52a17fb8c7: CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/39573073353 passes npm run release:check on Node 22 and 26, and bun run release:check on Node 26; every variant is 672/672 with zero fail/skip/cancel/todo and unchanged 100/100/100/100 coverage across all 46 sources. All other release and strict tracker-health checks pass; CodeQL run 39573073352 passes. Final-source pinned linked focused test passes 8/8. Repeated reader-body revert proofs preserve required imports/internal export, both typecheck, and fail 3/4 and 1/4 current descriptor tests; reverting the complete prior benchmark function typechecks and fails its 1/1 regression. Commands, timings and source identity are in docs/checkpoint-revert-evidence.json. Two local full attempts were intentionally interrupted (source correction; redundancy after CI passes), not counted as passing; no timeout observed. Existing history remains byte-identical with append-only additions. Only PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6ur6XM was unresolved; it is valid and fixed, including the same-class benchmark read found during whole-PR review. No new PM CLI/SDK defect encountered. Final evidence update changes only docs and tracker records. Leaving in progress for orchestrator verification, releasing claim; no thread replies/resolutions, mentions, merge or release. Substantive final-head review remains pending."
  "2026-10-21T10:13:26.024Z",codex-agent,"Review round on PR #92 at 3352546f28a9cfe04355f172f47495244032ce95: fetched every unresolved thread with all comments; pagination exhausted. Latest substantive CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Three valid small changes: batch ledger roots, benchmark import guard for unavailable launcher paths, and named missing-tool diagnostics. Preserve strict shared release launcher behavior. Plan retained regressions, independent behavioral revert proofs, whole-PR defect-class review, unchanged npm and Bun release gates with isolated Git identity, then explicit-path commit and push. No thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-10-21T10:17:18.326Z",codex-agent,"Five focused regressions pass directly and via pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress. Same-class self-review found transitive benchmark imports also reject unavailable launcher entries. Moved pure live configuration into scripts/meta-configuration.ts, preserved its existing re-export, and opted benchmark plus three trainer launchers into tolerant entry resolution. Shared release launcher remains strict by default; regressions explicitly verify this and a missing module path still throws. Real plain-directory tracker regression verifies one complete content-addressed ledger root, blob deduplication, publication failure cleanup, retry idempotence and GC retention. Missing ps and getconf diagnostics retain their original causes."
  "2026-10-21T10:18:55.443Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof receipt: docs/checkpoint-revert-evidence.json batch_launcher_review_round. Eight independent isolated behavioral reverts all typecheck and each fails one retained assertion test (exit 1): encodeCheckpointArtifacts per-blob ledger; checkpointToolBin missing-tool diagnostic; checkpointBenchmarkMain launcher guard; isMainInvocation tolerant behavior; benchmark transitive live import; prefixTrainerMain, referenceTrainerMain and lmTrainerMain guards. Exact commands: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"checkpoint batch publication\" test/checkpoint-artifacts.test.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"restricted process tools name\" test/checkpoint-artifacts.test.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"non-file launcher\" test/checkpoint-artifacts.test.ts. Production source was never reverted. Fixed focused suite passes 5/5 directly and through pinned pm test."
  "2026-10-21T10:19:00.510Z",codex-agent,Optional strict tracker health is separate from the required release gate and currently fails on extension host skew and merge-fence drift; existing follow-up pm-rl-9uz4 records the diagnostic alongside its existing stale-item and legacy-provenance advisories. No history repair or dependency-pin change performed.
  "2026-10-21T10:20:14.657Z",codex-agent,"Whole-PR self-review also bounded the newly batched ledger metadata before any publication. Otherwise an oversized batch or key could create a permanent root that the bounded reader cannot read. Added a real plain-tracker regression covering both oversized reference arrays and keys, with zero publication attempts. Stopped the initial full npm gate as superseded before this final correction; it is not counted as passing. Restarting unchanged full release gates against final source."
  "2026-10-21T10:21:42.888Z",codex-agent,"Final focused suite passes 6/6 directly and via pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress, including oversized ledger arrays and keys. The first size-bound regression fixture had 4096 references, which still fit the limit; corrected it to 8192 distinct references and reverified the fixed behavior before recording final revert evidence. Final full npm gate is in integration coverage; thresholds remain unchanged. Independent revert proofs are rerunning against this exact final test fixture."
  "2026-10-21T10:22:46.841Z",codex-agent,"Final-source behavioral revert proof is complete: nine independent variants in docs/checkpoint-revert-evidence.json all typecheck (exit 0) and fail retained regression assertions (exit 1). Restoring per-blob encodeCheckpointArtifacts fails 2/2 selected batch checks; removing only the ledger-size guard fails 1/1 oversized-metadata check. The missing-tool helper revert fails 1/1, and each of six launcher/configuration reverts fails 1/1. Fixed focused suite passes 6/6 directly and through the pinned runner. Both edited history streams preserve their previous byte prefixes; added tracked lines contain no absolute local paths. Publishing the source/proof commit for exact-head CI while the local full npm gate continues; full gate results are pending."
  "2026-10-21T10:42:52.756Z",codex-agent,"Final source 67b8f85bfbd427185fc3538f00ad32af761a4638 is validated by CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/39584178627: npm run release:check on Node 22 and 26 and bun run release:check on Node 26 each pass 676/676, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, unchanged 100 percent statements/lines/branches/functions across 47 sources, and all 336 declarations documented. All complete-gate stages, strict fresh-checkout tracker health and Bun installation pass; CodeQL run 39584179554 passes. Focused checks pass 6/6 directly and through pinned pm test. Nine final-source behavioral reverts typecheck and fail retained assertions; exact commands and timings are in docs/checkpoint-revert-evidence.json. All three original unresolved threads are valid and fixed, including the same-class transitive launcher and oversized-ledger findings from whole-PR review. No Outside diff range findings were present. Two local full npm attempts were deliberately stopped (superseded source; redundancy after required CI passes); neither is a pass, and no local timeout was observed. Local optional tracker-health drift remains in existing follow-up pm-rl-9uz4. No new PM CLI/SDK defect encountered. Final follow-up changes only documentation and tracker records; executable source/tests/pins/gate configuration stay identical to validated source. Leaving in progress for orchestrator verification and releasing the claim. No thread replies/resolutions, mentions, merge or release."
  "2026-10-21T19:36:28.216Z",codex-agent,"Authorized tracker reconciliation, audit 2026-10-21. Owner-authorized takeover of any historical assignment for this verified terminal transition. Reverified current main ce948522e18a: merged #92 (ce94852); source tree exactly matches the audited snapshot. **Lift the prefix learner's capacity bound: content-addressed checkpoint artifacts instead of the 4096-byte staging record.** [PR #92](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/92) (ce94852) stores large checkpoints as content-addressed blobs and retains checked receipt digests; capacity/corruption regressions and measured acceptance are committed."
